    {
      "id": "2073979887468306461",
      "text": "$4.7 billion. That is what Anthropic spent training Claude Fable 5.\n\nFor context, the entire global AI research budget in 2015 was $1.2 billion. One model now costs 4x what the entire field cost a decade ago.\n\nThis creates a moat, but not the one people think. The moat is not the model quality. GPT-5.6 and Gemini 3.5 Pro are within 8 points.\n\nThe moat is the capital barrier. Nobody new can enter this game without $4B+. That means the frontier model market is locked at 4 players: OpenAI, Anthropic, Google, Meta (open-source).\n\nStartups building on top of these models are renting their foundation. One price change from OpenAI kills their margins.\n\nBuild infrastructure, not wrappers.",
      "author": {
        "id": "1698152542868213760",
        "name": "Vivek Kotecha",
        "screenName": "vbkotecha",
